  "note": "Independent numpy implementation from: technicalindicators 3.1.0 (MIT), lib/candlestick/TweezerBottom.js and TweezerTop.js: a pattern needs 5 bars; over the closes of the window's first three bars, averagegain and averageloss with period 2 (the mean of the two positive moves, and of the two negative ones); a bottom when the average loss is above the average gain and the last two lows are equal, a top when the average gain is above the average loss and the last two highs are equal. The library compares averagegain's and averageloss's result ARRAYS with `>`, which JavaScript does on their strings (\"9\" > \"10\"); the reference compares the numbers, as the rule means. NaN before the fifth bar (the library needs 5); 100 for a bottom, -100 for a top, 0 elsewhere. On the shared bars it fires only on the flat stretch (bars 200 to 214), once each.",
